<input>
project name: flac
function signature: void FLAC::Decoder::FuzzerStream::metadata_callback(const FLAC__StreamMetadata *)
</input>

<description>
The metadata_callback function is a virtual method that is part of the FLAC::Decoder::FuzzerStream class. It is called by the FLAC decoder when it encounters a metadata block in the input stream. The function takes a single argument, `metadata`, which is a pointer to a `FLAC__StreamMetadata` struct. The function first performs some memory safety checks on the fields of the `metadata` struct. It then checks the `type` field of the struct to determine the type of the metadata block. Based on the type, it creates a new object of the corresponding metadata class (e.g., `Metadata::StreamInfo`, `Metadata::Padding`, etc.). It then performs some checks on the cloned object and deletes it.
</description>

<requirements>

<requirement>
The metadata argument should be a valid pointer to a FLAC__StreamMetadata struct. This is because the function dereferences this pointer to access its members.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `type` field of the `FLAC__StreamMetadata` struct should be one of the valid `FLAC__MetadataType` enum values. This is to ensure that the correct metadata object is created.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `is_last` field of the `FLAC__StreamMetadata` struct should be a boolean value. This is because it is used in a boolean context.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `length` field of the `FLAC__StreamMetadata` struct should be the correct length of the metadata block. This is to prevent out-of-bounds memory accesses.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `data` field of the `FLAC__StreamMetadata` struct should be a valid pointer to the metadata block data. This is because the function accesses this data to create the metadata object.
</requirement>

</requirements>

</function-requirements>

